                      SCFT
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#ReferencesEngineeringOfTopologicalOrderOnM5s"} Engineering of topological order on M5s
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The embedding (meaning: realization) of aspects of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            (QFTs) into/within sectors of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            — where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            happens near
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+singularities"} orbifold singularities
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-planes"} O-planes
            and/or on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolumes"} worldvolumes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            (e.g.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            in a useful way. For instance the various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dualities of string theory
            will relate different QFTs in way that are typically far from obvious from just looking at these QFTs themselves.
          %p
            The investigation specifically of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D1+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=1 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            in this fashion has come to be known as
            %em geometric engineering of quantum field theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#KatzKlemmVafa97"}> Katz, Klemm &amp; Vafa 1997
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#KatzKlemm96"} Katz-Klemm 96
          %p
            Specifically, the geometrically engineered QFTs are those on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            that end on (are suspended between)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HananyWitten97"} Hanany-Witten 97
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Fazzi17"} Fazzi 17
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "NS5-brane#DBranesEndingOnNS5Branes"} D-branes ending on NS5-branes
          %p
            Beware that the term “geometric engineering” is often associated specifically to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbi-singular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+spacetime"} bulk
            dynamics.
          %p
            The alternative term “
            %strong> brane engineering
            ” &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#GómezHernández98"}> Gómez &amp; Hernández 1998
            \&amp;rbrack; refers more generally to the realization of aspects of QTFs in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
          %p
            But since there are in general also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbi-singularities
            on the brane, it makes sense to broadly speak of
            = succeed "." do
              %em geometric brane engineering of QFTs
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large N limit
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coincident+branes"} coincident branes
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+spacetime"} bulk spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            in the guise of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            For more relations between QFTs found via string theory see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+results+applied+elsewhere"} string theory results applied elsewhere
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Holographic+M-Brane+Super-Embeddings"} GSS25
          %div{:style => "margin:-35px 0px 00px 00px;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ProbeBraneEmbedding.png", :width => "900"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Fazzi17"} Fazzi 17, pp. 25, 32
          %div{:style => "margin:-30px 0px 00px 00px;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HananyWittenConfig.png"}/
          %div{:style => "margin:-30px 0px 00px 00px;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HananyWittenConfigII.png"}/
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
